            "UID": "0x11f1830f39c2a7ca830f025041000001",
            "NAME": "Read logs",
            "ALIAS": "LogsRead",
            "DESCRIPTION": "Read log details, search log files",
            "APP": "0x11efbd2d8f0ae0babd2dc84bd653ed63",
            "INSTRUCTIONS": [
                "// Multiline text delimited by `\n`",
                "# Reading the logs",
                "",
                "The workbench has a central logger, that will save all logs as CSV files in `<installation>/logs/<yyyy-mm-dd>.<version>.log`. A log entry is represented as a csv line. Each log message has a unique Log-ID and consists of the CSV line and a JSON file with log details. The details files are located in `logs/details/<yyyy-mm-dd>/<Log-ID>.json`.",
                "",
                "CSV structure:",
                "",
                "1. KEY_DATETIME",
                "2. Log-ID",
                "3. Request-ID (X-Request-ID header)",
                "4. Log-level (numeric)",
                "5. Log-level (verbose)",
                "6. Channel",
                "7. Username (if known at the time of logging)",
                "8. Action alias (if known at the time of logging)",
                "9. Log message",
                "",
                "Use the Log-ID to fetch all details for a log entry via `GetLogDetails`. Log details are very verbose: each message will contain a lot of details about the state of the workbench. Error messages will also contain links to the documentation pages related to the error.",
                "",
                "Use `SearchLogs` to search for Request-ID to find all log lines related to this request. If an error occurs, the logger writes a lot of additional information with different log levels collected during the request. In particular, these log items are of interest:",
                "",
                "- `HTTP request ... received` - contains a dump of the HTTP request received",
                "- `Authorized...` messages contain information about security policies evaluated to check access to something",
                "- `Action ... performed` contains detailed action logbooks",
                "- `Query ...` messages contain SQL, web service requests and other data source queries.",
                "",
                "The `SearchLogs` tool will do a plain file search in the CSV logs - you can search for messages, usernames, request ids - anything."
            ],
            "CONFIG_UXON": {
                "tools": {
                    "GetLogDetails": {
                        "alias": "axenox.GenAI.GetLogEntryTool",
                        "description": "Read another log entry by providing its Log-ID"
                    },
                    "SearchLogs": {
                        "alias": "axenox.GenAI.FileSearchTool",
                        "description": "Search the CSV log files",
                        "use_vendor_folder_as_base": false,
                        "allowed_paths": [
                            "logs/*.log"
                        ],
                        "arguments": [
                            {
                                "name": "path",
                                "description": "Folder to search in. Always use `logs/`"
                            },
                            {
                                "name": "name",
                                "description": "Optional filename pattern (glob) for log files"
                            },
                            {
                                "name": "query",
                                "description": "Optional string or regular expression to search for in log file contents.",
                                "examples": [
                                    "/->(CreateData|UpdateData)\\(.*/i"
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                }
            },
